 (report . "Round 5 review (independent, read-only VERIFY subagent) against implementation head ba35b090f78f00cc287133f2b77792fa836919cd (content digest ca5174f339b0ef53dbfc404aa9b16be88e8d7bca3feca1582b8a99b2b8d311e8) returned REQUEST_CHANGES with one blocking traceability defect: the declared W4 recovery artifacts (activation.json, rollback-drill.json) and the activation report still named head f05c21bce, which predates the round-3/4 compiled-root CLI and lane changes, so they no longer described the delivered code and broke the evidence identity/history requirement. It was fixed by re-running the retained drill harness against the committed CLI at the repaired head: all five phases pass (producer build+publish, consumer verified root hit with zero eager compiles, global-off rollback with one eager compile at 481 ms, current-source canary refusing the stale root with one eager compile at 480 ms and output 63, and tamper canary refusing the flipped manifest with one eager compile at 480 ms and output 42). activation.json, rollback-drill.json, the raw transcript and the report were re-derived and SHA256SUMS rebound; the artifact-provenance lint exits 0. The round-4 code fixes (off-lane bounded eager gate, two-axis telemetry classification, producer/fallback cost plumbing, telemetry upload after launch) and the round-3 wiring fixes were confirmed present. The declared Verify chain is green (182 focused tests, arch 32/32, security 64/64, workflows 33/33, check-deps, metrics --lint, provenance lint, fast 1208/1208) and retained at raw/verify-chain.txt. The trio is now bound at implementation head d9157cf2d148b74b4b0bf4c5452e42f88e183dce with content digest 0bd809cd4ee0bed07232f59d2000a4f7c5a805249c52235b4b370d6c12940bf4. History: rounds 1-4 findings (producer input, zero-module run, linear history; then five W2-hygiene findings; then four lane-wiring defects; then the off-lane eager gate and honest W4 telemetry) were all fixed and are recorded in the red-first captures and the repair narrative."))